# Keep the repository's text as it was written: LF, everywhere.
#
# bin/sync.mjs is a command: npm links it into .bin and the OS executes it
# through its shebang. A checkout that turned its lines into CRLF — which
# is what git's core.autocrlf=true does by default on Windows — leaves
# "#!/usr/bin/env node\r", and the kernel hunts for an interpreter literally
# named "node\r": `env: 'node\r': No such file or directory`, exit 127. The
# file still runs under `node file.mjs` (the JS engine tolerates CRLF), so
# this only breaks the paths that matter: a symlinked bin, a global install
# on WSL/Cygwin, and anyone running it directly.
#
# So: text is text, in LF. Marked explicitly rather than with `* text=auto`
# so binary files stay untouched, and so this file's intent is readable.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly binary: never convert, never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.tgz binary
